{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"components","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [[","kind":"text"},{"text":"VehicleComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:10TripKitAPI5TKAPIV17VehicleComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/TripKitAPI\/documentation\/TripKitAPI\/TKAPI\/VehicleComponents"},{"text":"]]?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["iOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The top level array represents connected parts of the vehicle, which you can’t walk through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without leaving the vehicle (e.g., two trains connected together). The inner level array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represents then parts that can be walked through (e.g., the carriages of a train). A bus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would have a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[[component1]]"},{"type":"text","text":". A train could have "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[[c1, c2, c3, c4], [c5, c6, c7, c8]]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrays are ordered by direction of travel always being left-to-right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"i.e., the front of the train is the very last element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"components","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:10TripKitAPI5TKAPIV7VehicleV10componentsSaySayAC0E10ComponentsVGGSgvp","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"components","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [[","kind":"text"},{"text":"VehicleComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s: